From: arttttt <artem-bambalov@yandex.ru>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 04:17:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] taskbar: off unless the user turns it on

On a large screen the taskbar was on until the user turned it off. On
mocha, which navigates with its keys, the owner wants the phone's
layout: the taskbar now starts off, and the switch in the button
settings still turns it on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/com/android/launcher3/DeviceProfile.java | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/com/android/launcher3/DeviceProfile.java b/src/com/android/launcher3/DeviceProfile.java
index e61f7f9..516225f 100644
--- a/src/com/android/launcher3/DeviceProfile.java
+++ b/src/com/android/launcher3/DeviceProfile.java
@@ -272,8 +272,10 @@ public class DeviceProfile {
         }
 
         hotseatQsbHeight = res.getDimensionPixelSize(R.dimen.qsb_widget_height);
+        // Off unless chosen, on mocha's tablet as on a phone: the device navigates
+        // with its keys, and the taskbar is the user's to turn on.
         boolean isTaskBarEnabled = LineageSettings.System.getInt(context.getContentResolver(),
-                LineageSettings.System.ENABLE_TASKBAR, isTablet ? 1 : 0) == 1;
+                LineageSettings.System.ENABLE_TASKBAR, 0) == 1;
         isTaskbarPresent = isTaskBarEnabled && ApiWrapper.TASKBAR_DRAWN_IN_PROCESS
                 && FeatureFlags.ENABLE_TASKBAR.get();
         if (isTaskbarPresent) {
